About Essencemediacom: A Leading WPP Media Brand

Essesncemediacom is a new breed of media agency. Grounded in analytics &amp; insights, and powered by data &amp; technology, we believe in the power of media and creative to drive breakthroughs for the world's best brands. We help clients understand the modern marketing paradox and discover the breakthroughs brands need to win with their consumers. We are designed for the new communications economy - built on data &amp; technology, built for people &amp; algorithms, built around diverse schools of thought, built to test &amp; learn at scale, and, crucially, built to evolve.

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

The Senior Associate, Media will lead the development and execution of&nbsp;360&nbsp;media strategies to enhance the company's online presence, drive engagement, and achieve marketing goals,&nbsp;ultimately driving&nbsp;significant growth and brand awareness for our clients. This role is ideal for someone with at least one year&nbsp;and a half&nbsp;of experience in digital media, who is ready to take on more responsibility, manage projects, and contribute to strategic planning.  &nbsp;

• Develop and implement comprehensive digital media strategies to support marketing&nbsp;objectives&nbsp;and enhance brand visibility.     &nbsp;

• Analyze&nbsp;market trends and user data to inform strategy and make data-driven decisions.     &nbsp;

• Design, execute, and oversee digital campaigns across multiple channels, including social media, email marketing, and digital advertising.     &nbsp;

• Manage the end-to-end process of digital media campaigns from concept to execution, including budget management and performance tracking.     &nbsp;

• Develop and manage a content calendar that aligns with marketing goals and audience interests.     &nbsp;

• Collaborate with internal teams and external partners to create high-quality, engaging content.     &nbsp;

• Plan and manage paid digital advertising campaigns, display ads, and social media ads.     &nbsp;

• Track,&nbsp;analyze, and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) for all digital media activities.     &nbsp;

• Provide insights and recommendations based on performance data to improve campaign effectiveness and ROI.     &nbsp;

Skills and Experience &nbsp;

At WPP Media, we believe in the power of our culture and our people.&nbsp;It’s&nbsp;what elevates us to deliver exceptional experiences for both our clients and each other. In this role it will be critical to embrace WPP &amp; WPP Media’s shared core values: &nbsp;

• Be Extraordinary by Leading Collectively to Inspire transformational Creativity. &nbsp;

• Create an Open environment by Balancing People and Client Experiences by Cultivating Trust. &nbsp;

• Lead Optimistically by Championing Growth and Development to Mobilize the Enterprise. &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Communications, Digital Media, or a related field.   &nbsp;

• Minimum of 1 year&nbsp;and a half&nbsp;of experience in digital media, marketing, or a related role.   &nbsp;

• Proven experience with digital media platforms&nbsp;and campaign management.   &nbsp;

• Strong understanding of social media and digital advertising strategies.   &nbsp;

• Proficiency&nbsp;in digital marketing tools and analytics platforms (social media insights).   &nbsp;

Du wirst Teil eines KI-nativen Start-ups in einer frühen Entwicklungsphase, dessen Produkt seinen Product-Market-Fit bereits unter Beweis gestellt hat. Wir entwickeln modernste KI-Lösungen für Governance, Risikomanagement und Compliance (GRC) für Unternehmen weltweit.
Unsere Kunden sind Auditoren, Risikomanager und Compliance-Teams. Deshalb sind gründliche Evaluierung, Auditierbarkeit und die Vorbereitung auf die Anforderungen der EU-KI-Verordnung für uns keine nachträglichen Ergänzungen, sondern feste Produktanforderungen.
Aufgaben
Als Anwendungsarchitekt (m/w/d) gehörst du zu unseren ersten Senior-Entwicklern in Vollzeit und arbeitest eng mit unserem Mitgründer und CTO zusammen. Du verantwortest die Backend-Architektur und hilfst dem Team, Qualität und Entwicklungsgeschwindigkeit mit dem Wachstum zu steigern.
In den ersten 6-12 Monaten wirst du:

eine klare Zielarchitektur und eine solide Dokumentationsgrundlage mit arc42 etablieren;
das zentrale Domänenmodell anhand von DDD-Prinzipien präzisieren und im Team vermitteln;
einen KI-getriebenen Entwicklungsprozess einführen und standardisieren - von der Feature-Spezifikation bis zur Bereitstellung in der Produktionsumgebung;
die Entwicklungspraxis durch Coaching, Pair Programming und Feedbackschleifen stärken, insbesondere für Junior-Entwickler;
die Zuverlässigkeit und Softwareauslieferung durch bessere CI/CD-Prozesse , Testautomatisierung und eine sauber gepflegte Infrastruktur verbessern.

Verantwortlichkeiten

Gemeinsam mit dem Team überzeugende Lösungen für neuartige Problemstellungen in einer AI-first-Architektur entwickeln.
Einen DevOps-orientierten Ansatz über den gesamten Lebenszyklus hinweg vorantreiben: von der Spezifikation über die Entwicklung bis zur Ausliefe

About EXANTE

EXANTE is a wealth tech company that provides centralized trading solutions and B2B financial infrastructure that helps create value through technology.
Our proprietary trading platform enables direct market access to 1M financial instruments from a single multi-currency account, including stocks, ETFs, bonds, futures, and options.
We are a fast-growing global company with 600+ employees across 70+ locations, representing 60 nationalities, all of us following the same guiding principles:
We believe that freedom is an inherited right
We are catalysts
We defend privacy
We cater to our customers to an unprecedented degree
As a Financial company, we know our investment priorities. We invest in our people.
Join us in creating a new standard for wealth management:
Location: Remotely
Worksite: Remotely
Key responsibilities:

• Support of the existing extensive code base (microservices);
· Development of external connection points to the trading system: backend for interfaces, HTTP API, FIX API;
· Optimization and modification of the architecture of existing infrastructure in order to increase productivity and facilitate further maintenance.

Requirements:

• 3+ years of Scala development experience;
· Knowledge of various JVM multithreading models (blocking, CAS, Future/Promise, Actors);
· Understanding of the basic ideas of functional programming (recursion, laziness, pure functions);
· Knowledge and ability to work with scala collections, understanding of for-comprehensions;
· Experience with the akka library (akka-http, akka-streams, actor model);
· Knowledge of basic data structures and basic algorithms;

· Experience with SQL;

• Ability to write tests and understanding the need for this;
· Independence and responsibility in work.

The advantages will be:
· experience in a fintech company;
· trading experience and knowledge of financial mathematics;
· experience in writing multi-threaded, high-load systems.

